    "specialization": "The public literal matcher defaults to a block-level single-character IndexOf(char) loop only for sensitive, non-whole-word one-character literals. Longer literals continue through the prior SearchValues first-character filter, SequenceEqual verification and stateful tail handling.",
    "fallback": "Case-insensitive, whole-word, newline-containing and longer-literal paths retain their existing scalar/stateful behavior. No custom SIMD or architecture-specific intrinsic was added; the BCL span primitive supplies runtime feature dispatch and scalar fallback.",
